import pathlib,json,hashlib,re,datetime,subprocess
L=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];E=json.loads((L/'outputs/extracted.json').read_text());R=json.loads((L/'reservation.json').read_text());results={}
# Dispositions deliberately distinguish a reported solution from a body-verified full-scope result.
D={
349310:('parked_bounded_search','Source Eq. (3), Conjecture 30; current arXiv v2, corresponding published Conjecture 35.','The literal word is the fixed point 0 -> 0^p 1^q, 1 -> 1^p 0^q. C sweeps found no progression exceeding the piecewise bound. Prefix searches cannot establish a maximum over every starting position. Composite Q is the source-identified weak regime; second pass expands p,q and prefixes.','Uniform bound over all starts and all d <= (p+q)^n+1, including composite-base nontrivial gcd cases.','outputs/words.log; outputs/words2.log; scripts/words.c; scripts/words2.c','finite word witness low; full automatic-sequence bound high'),
354350:('parked_bounded_numeric_search','Source Conjecture 4.1 and preceding scope; spectral construction.','Twelve applicable graph/parameter cases in the atlas through order 7, odd edge counts only, give no numerical violation. Checked absence of short odd cycles by DFS. The construction replaces an edge by a path with 2k-1 internal vertices. Even m makes the printed bipartite part nonintegral; no credit claimed from that defect.','New exact spectral violation in meaningful integer domain, or full general bound with source domain resolved.','outputs/odd-spectral.json; scripts/odd_spectral.py','moderate for rational spectral witness; high for full theorem'),
355274:('parked_bounded_exact_search','Source definitions, Conjectures 2 and 3, introductory known classes.','Exact subset dynamic programming computes the minimum number of locally irregular edge classes for every connected atlas graph of orders 2 through 6. No colorable graph needs more than 3 in this range. The bow-tie refutes the old three-color conjecture, not this four-color bound; metadata refuted status conflates them.','A colorable graph needing at least 5 classes, or a full four-color construction. No extension from the source cactus results found.','outputs/local-irregular.json; scripts/finite.py','low for finite coloring certificate; high for full graph theorem'),
355998:('parked_semantic_formalization_gap','Definitions 3 and 4, Proposition 5, Conjecture 6, Theorem 1 graph description.','The conjecture minimizes over actual successive symplectic rational blowdowns, not merely paths in the authors combinatorial graph. Proposition 5 supplies an upper bound only. Finite graph calculations would not certify a lower bound against every geometric blowdown sequence.','Geometric lower bound by number of interior ones; bridge from all blowdown operations to combinatorial depth.','sources/355998.txt','very high; symplectic topology semantics'),
357156:('parked_bounded_exact_search','Theorem 1, Corollary 8, Sections 4.6 and 4.7, Conjecture 25.','Enumerated sorted reciprocal-denominator tuples with all di >= 2 and integral reciprocal sum: n=4,5,6 with denominator <= 1000000; n=7 <= 100; n=8 <= 40. Source group formula yields cyclic iff no prime divides four denominators. Maximum cyclic orders found are 6,42,1806,546,630; no violation. The first three match conjectured values; later caps exclude the doubly exponential extremal example. Values di=1 reduce to a smaller star. Source already enumerated groups through n=7; baseline repetition is not progress.','All-denominator sharp cyclic order bound, or targeted n>=8 tuple exceeding a_(n-1). Bounded small denominators are far from decisive.','outputs/star.json; scripts/star.py','moderate for finite Smith-form certificate, high for uniform bound'),
358614:('parked_unbounded_quantifiers','Conjecture 30; definitions of o-cliques, absolute and relative clique numbers; Theorem 9 and Erdős-Hajnal context.','Polynomial tau-boundedness quantifies over an unknown polynomial and all graph orders. A single small acyclic graph cannot refute it. The paper gives conditional/quasipolynomial machinery and D_k subset R_(k^2+1); a finite catalogue would not settle the polynomial gap.','Uniform polynomial bound, or a superpolynomial family with bounded absolute/relative clique parameter.','sources/358614.txt','high; no finite witness to polynomial nonexistence'),
360261:('excluded_source_refutation','Conjecture 10, Lemma 11, Theorems 12 and 13 with proof paragraphs.','The source itself disproves the conjecture for k=q-3 and k=q-2: the codes are MDS, with distances 3 and 2 respectively, rather than 1-MDS. Theorem 13 treats 3 <= k <= q-4. The proof computes zero-sum subset counts and applies Lemma 11. This is an existing source resolution, not a new code discovery.','None for exclusion; no independent formal replay of published proof claimed.','sources/360261.txt','not invested; source already resolves'),
360775:('parked_unknown_constant','Source final higher-dimensional discussion and Conjecture 5.','There exists c(d)<1 and an unspecified big-O multiplicative constant, uniformly over minimal fillings. One finite complex cannot refute those unknown constants. Even enumerating fillings exactly gives only diagnostics without an unbounded family. The earlier shortest-path theorem and triangulated-sphere proposition do not supply the requested higher-dimensional estimate.','An all-scale irreducible-cycle family saturating base Delta, or a uniform higher-dimensional counting argument.','sources/360775.txt','high; homology plus asymptotic family'),
362021:('excluded_published_refutation','Source Conjecture 4.9; Das-Roy-Saha arXiv:2405.15897 Theorem 5.3 and Remark 5.4, actual construction and colon-ideal proof.','The successor explicitly refutes Hang-Vu Conjecture 4.9 even for trees. Attach k disjoint 2-edge arms to the end of a (t-2)-vertex path. The colon ideal is generated by k disjoint quadratic monomials, giving regularity at least k while nu_t=1. The gap is arbitrarily large for every t>=4. No fresh search after this published construction was identified.','None for exclusion.','sources/path-prior.txt; sources/362021.txt','not invested; published exact refutation'),
366209:('parked_unknown_linear_constant','Source Theorems 1.1, 1.2, 1.3 and Introduction.','The source refutes the 2k-connectivity conjecture but proves a 10^7 k^4 out-degree sufficient bound at 2k+1 connectivity. That does not prove or refute existence of a linear constant C in the reserved statement. A small non-linked tournament excludes only small choices of C.','Uniform linear-degree linkage proof or family of (2k+1)-connected non-k-linked tournaments with delta+/k unbounded.','sources/366209.txt','high; routing disjoint paths plus unbounded k'),
366300:('parked_small_order_residual','Conjecture 1.1, Theorem 1.1 and its specialization; definition of kite graph.','The actual source proves the conjecture for sufficiently large n, with n threshold unspecified here; it does not settle every n>=5. Numerical Jacobi diagonalization checked 1330 graph/alpha cases: all connected atlas graphs n=5,6 and alpha=0.50,0.55,...,0.95. No violation above tolerance 1e-7. No numerical outcome is an exact certificate.','Resolve remaining small orders uniformly in alpha or produce a rational spectral separation with exact proof.','outputs/spectral.json; scripts/finite.py','moderate for finite witness; high for uniform eigenvalue analysis'),
366396:('excluded_published_refutation','Original Conjecture 8.3; Araujo-Xiang arXiv:2507.13267 Theorem 1.6, Proposition 2.1, Claims 2.2 and 2.3, proof bodies.','The published five-vertex oriented graph S with arcs 12,13,23,24,34,35,41,52 is Turanable and embeds in no D_s. Read the triangle-part contradiction and the semiregular near-tournament counting proof. This is the exact same characterization and a public refutation.','None for exclusion.','sources/turan-prior.txt','not invested; published exact refutation'),
367084:('parked_source_reported_resolution_with_scope_limit','Original Conjecture 7.2 and subsequent-work note; Iarovikova-Kupavskii arXiv:2507.17913 Theorem 1.','Original source says the conjecture was proved. Actual successor Theorem 1 has n>=n0, uniformly in 2<=t<=n-2, and proves the balanced fixed-forest family (j=0) extremal. This does not on its face settle every small n in the literal all-n wording. Exhaustive maximum-clique computations over all labelled spanning trees verify n=3,4,5 and all 1<=t<=n-1. No full all-n settlement asserted.','Bridge or published theorem covering the finitely many but unspecified small orders; otherwise a small-n violation or full proof.','sources/trees-prior-actual.txt; outputs/small-trees.json; scripts/small_trees.py','moderate for finite witness; high for full extremal theorem'),
367365:('parked_generic_rank_gap','Conjecture 9 (published Conjecture 4.1), factorization B=C R, Example 11, Rado equivalent formulation.','Computed specialized rigidity and squared-area derivative ranks mod 1000003. All 1024 triangle subfamilies on 5 vertices agree with the Rado rank prediction at one sampled coordinate set. Sixteen sampled 10-triangle complexes on n=6..9 also agree. This is specialization evidence only: modular ranks are not proofs of generic rational rank equalities or deficiencies. Source Example 11 fails the Hall condition and is not a counterexample to this conjecture.','A rank defect persisting generically while the standard rigidity Rado condition holds, or a general generic-rank theorem.','outputs/rigidity.json; scripts/rigidity.py','high; literal generic matroid semantics and symbolic upper rank certificate'),
367689:('parked_source_corrected_exact_search','Source y_G definition before Theorem 1.3; Theorem 1.5, Lemmas 2.1-2.2, Theorem 3.2 and Conjecture 4.2; companion 2204.08010 Theorem 2.2 proof.','MathDB calls y_G the maximum partial-dual genus, but the source defines y_G=max_A(2c(G-A)-|A|-1), a deficiency, and genus=n-y_G. Checked the actual source conjecture. Exhaustive set-partition checks on 773 applicable connected planar atlas graphs through n=7 found no violation. Independent subset-partition DP checked 100 seeded connected planar graphs n=8..12, also no violation. Source/cited bridges were read; no qualifying full proof found.','Universal deficiency/clique-cover bound or a new exact planar witness. The paraphrase mismatch alone is excluded.','outputs/partial-dual-atlas.json; outputs/planar.json; scripts/atlas.py; scripts/planar.py','low for finite cut/clique-cover witness; moderate/high for uniform structural theorem'),
370754:('parked_asymptotic_spectral_gap','Source Theorem 4.1 discussion, Conjecture 5.1, Problems 5.2 and 5.3.','The metadata solution quote concerns the Erdos pentagon theorem, not this Conjecture 5.1. Its conclusion is eventually in n, with a real spectral maximization and arbitrary forbidden family. Small n cannot refute an unspecified n0. The source minimum-coordinate estimate or spectral-increment expansion would imply the conjecture but are posed as problems.','Uniform principal-eigenvector lower-coordinate bound or controlled spectral-increment expansion, with all family assumptions.','sources/370754.txt','very high; analytic spectral semantics and asymptotic quantifiers'),
371286:('excluded_public_registry_refutation','Source Conjecture 1, Theorem 4 construction, Theorem 12; live Omega KochNarayanRefutation.lean actual definitions and proof.','Own capped greedy edge-addition search found printed-bound violations at (n,gamma)=(15,4),(16,4),(17,4),(18,4). The source construction has a Phi/count inconsistency; unbalancing dominator sides already improves the bound, an excluded source-ingredient bridge. Independently, current public Omega has a complete 14-vertex 28-edge witness against bound26, unique gamma4, plus proof of the universal negation. Read actual Lean source; did not rebuild it. Existing public refutation decisively rules out discovery investment.','None for exclusion. No priority date for the public commit asserted; current public proof is enough to stop this route.','sources/public-KochNarayanRefutation.lean; sources/public-KochNarayanRefutation.md; outputs/domination.json; scripts/domination.py','low but excluded by existing resolution and source-ingredient concern'),
372295:('parked_eventual_extremal_formula','Source Section 5 Conjecture 5.1, its theorem-range comparison and lower-bound construction comment.','The formula is claimed only for n>N_(ell,r,k). Finite small hypergraphs cannot refute the statement without an unbounded family. The indicator is defined by parity of ell in the preceding theorem (the extracted conjecture prints I_r). The printed n-k ell prime-1+1 term is retained in provenance, not silently repaired. No endpoint correction proposed as a discovery.','Infinite counterfamily exceeding the intended eventual bound, or a sharp all-large-n upper bound in the wider r range.','sources/372295.txt','high; hypergraph embeddings and eventual threshold'),
376111:('excluded_current_source_theorem','Current source Theorem 11 and Section 6 proof; line-graph Lemma 22 and cograph decomposition Lemma 23.','Current source proves exactly ex_lin_r(n,P4^r)<=(r+1)n/r for every r>=2 and the disjoint Steiner-system equality classification. Read theorem and proof opening; current abstract explicitly says it settles the proceedings conjecture. No new result from applying or formalizing this proof.','None for exclusion; no independent audit of the full published argument claimed.','sources/376111.txt','not invested; source now proves exact claim'),
376304:('parked_finite_geometry_boundary_search','Source Definitions 1.1 and Eq. (1), D_q formula, Theorem 1.3, Section 5 Conjecture 5.2 and both barriers.','Enumerated all 35 two-subspaces of F2^4 and all 30 maximal intersecting families; each has projective Ore degree3, equal to the two-barrier threshold. Monotonicity under adding members covers their subfamilies. For (q,n,k,s)=(2,6,2,3), the fixed-2space meeting family has sigma9 and fixed-5space clique has sigma15, matching the controlling barrier15. The source already prints the older single-barrier failure; that is not a new refutation of this corrected statement.','A nonstandard direct-sum-matching obstruction beyond both barriers or a sharp low-dimension extension of the source theorem.','outputs/geometry.json; scripts/geometry.py','moderate for explicit finite subspace certificate; high for general q,n,k,s')}
http=json.loads((L/'outputs/http-receipts.json').read_text())
for i in R['ids']:
 x=E[str(i)];r=x['record'];outcome,depth,attempt,gap,artifacts,cost=D[i]
 results[str(i)]={'mathdb_id':i,'title':r['title'],'canonical_url':r['canonical_url'],'literal_statement':r['statement'],'statement_sha256':hashlib.sha256(r['statement'].encode()).hexdigest(),'provenance':{k:x[k] for k in ['chunk','line','chunk_sha256','raw_sha256']},'raw_file':f'sources/{i}.raw.jsonl','source_url':r['source_url'],'source_receipts':[v for v in http if v['id']==i],'source_pdf_sha256':hashlib.sha256((L/f'sources/{i}.pdf').read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'current_version_metadata':re.findall(r'arXiv:[0-9.]+v[0-9]+', (L/f'sources/{i}.abs').read_text()),'review_depth':{'literal_statement':True,'primary_body_sections_read':depth,'full_proof_independently_audited':False,'formal_replay':False},'outcome':outcome,'mathematical_attempts':attempt,'remaining_lemmas_or_gaps':gap,'artifacts':artifacts.split('; '),'lean_cost':cost,'history_check':'Campaign ledger and inherited exclusions read; bounded prior-note ID path search retained in outputs/history-paths.txt. No old exclusion claimed absent globally. See outputs/historical-exact.txt for all 20 IDs.','novelty_limit':'Bounded primary and live registry checks only; path nonmatches are not proof absence. No literature novelty clearance or acceptance.','discovery_count_credit':0,'root_decision_required':True}
